<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umaru Dallaji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1835</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Umaru Dallaji was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> scholar and follower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a> who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> in Katsina, capturing the city from its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> ruler in 1807. He became the first emir of Katsina within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>, ruling until his death in 1835 and founding the Dallazawa dynasty. The deposed Hausa rulers withdrew north and eventually established the Sultanate of Maradi.</p></div>
